{"name":"African Violet","hex":"#b085b7","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"violet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant or flower of the genus Viola, especially the fragrant Viola odorata;  similar-looking plants and flowers.","A person thought to resemble V. odorata, especially in its beauty and delicacy."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a violet colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violet"}],"entries":[{"title":"African Violet (film)","blocks":[{"text":"African Violet is a 2019 Iranian drama film directed by Mona Zandi Haghighi and written by Haghighi and Hamidreza Bababeigi. The film screened for the first time at the 37th Fajr Film Festival and received 2 nominations."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1c/Africanvioletposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_Violet_(film)"},{"title":"African Violet (album)","blocks":[{"text":"African Violet is an album by American trumpeter Blue Mitchell which features arrangements by McKinley Mitchell recorded in 1977 and released on the Impulse! label in 1978."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e3/African_Violet_%28album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_Violet_(album)"},{"title":"Streptocarpus sect. Saintpaulia","blocks":[{"text":"Streptocarpus sect. Saintpaulia is a section within Streptocarpus subgenus Streptocarpella consisting of about ten species of herbaceous perennial flowering plants in the family Gesneriaceae, native to Tanzania and adjacent southeastern Kenya in eastern tropical Africa. The section was previously treated as a separate genus, Saintpaulia, but molecular phylogenetic studies showed that it was nested within the genus Streptocarpus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Saintpaulia_ionantha.jpg/330px-Saintpaulia_ionantha.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Streptocarpus_sect._Saintpaulia"},{"title":"Violet (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Violet is the color of light at the short wavelength end of the visible spectrum. It is one of the seven colors that Isaac Newton labeled when dividing the spectrum of visible light in 1704. Violet light has a wavelength between approximately 380 and 435 nanometers. The color's name is derived from the Viola genus of flowers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Amatista_Laye_2.jpg/330px-Amatista_Laye_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Violet_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/2007-04-20Saintpaulia_ionantha03.jpg/500px-2007-04-20Saintpaulia_ionantha03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/2007-04-20Saintpaulia_ionantha03.jpg/1280px-2007-04-20Saintpaulia_ionantha03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/2007-04-20Saintpaulia_ionantha03.jpg/500px-2007-04-20Saintpaulia_ionantha03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Streptocarpus ionanthus flowers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2007-04-20Saintpaulia_ionantha03.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Saintpaulia_%27Pink_Amiss%27_02.jpg/500px-Saintpaulia_%27Pink_Amiss%27_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Saintpaulia_%27Pink_Amiss%27_02.jpg/1280px-Saintpaulia_%27Pink_Amiss%27_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content